--TEST--
an interface's own declaration highlights nothing where a class below implements it, because an `implements` clause is no occurrence of the name it writes — the reference query at the same cursor answers the declaration alone for that same reason, `rule:ide/five-features-are-one-reference-index`
--FILE--
<?nvs
interface Gre<|>ets
{
    public function greet(): string;
}

class User implements Greets
{
    public function greet(): string
    {
        return "hi";
    }
}
--REQUEST--
documentHighlight
--EXPECT--
none
